Uninstall addons and remove them from the profile's config.

Only the folders Knapsack installed for each addon are deleted. An addon is
named by its ref or URL, or by its short name (baganator-mirror) when that
matches one addon.

Usage:
  knapsack remove <addon>... [flags]

Aliases:
  remove, rm

Examples:
  knapsack remove baganator-mirror
  knapsack rm github:austinrr/syndicator-mirror

Flags:
  -h, --help             help for remove
  -p, --profile string   profile to act on (default $KNAPSACK_PROFILE, then the current profile)

Global Flags:
      --config string   use this config file instead of the default
  -v, --verbose         show progress and the underlying cause of errors
